      "keyInsight": "The bullying narcissist sees the world as a rigid two-seater teeter-totter. In their eyes, there is no way for two people to stand on level ground together. If you are elevated, they feel like they are sinking into the mud. Therefore, the only way they can feel tall is to forcefully shove your side down to the asphalt. The dark paradox of the office or domestic bully is their total dependence on victims. Without someone else around to label as a pathetic loser, they have no mirror left to tell them they are a winner. Their entire sense of glory requires constant humiliation of the people beside them.",
