      "keyInsight": "Think of a parade balloon inflated to twenty times its normal size to float above skyscrapers. It looks towering, majestic, and completely untouchable from the street below. But all that impressive bulk is filled with thin, nervous air. One tiny pinprick can cause the whole spectacle to burst with a deafening screech. That is the grandiose narcissist. They constantly tell stories where they are the daring savior, the misunderstood genius, or the undisputed kingpin. They talk loudly over others at dinner tables and cut in traffic because regular rules are for ordinary mortals. The great irony is that this massive swagger exists purely to hide a terrifying inner secret: a paralyzing dread of being average. Their loud boasting is not authentic strength; it is a giant suit of cardboard armor.",
